# Support feats from Sword & Fist (3e) in 3.5 syntax, needed as prerequisites
# Source: The (mostly) Complete Dragon Magazine Compendium - Feats, Flaws & Styles (compendium pp. 1058-1176).
# DESC ends with the original Dragon Magazine issue and article. SOURCEPAGE = compendium PDF page.
# Prerequisites that could not be expressed as PCGen PRE tags are listed in PRETEXT.

Circle Kick	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	SOURCELONG:Sword & Fist	SOURCESHORT:SF	SOURCEPAGE:p.5	PRESTAT:1,DEX=15	PRETOTALAB:3	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Improved Unarmed Strike	DESC:You kick multiple opponents with the same attack action. [Sword & Fist feat, included in 3.5 syntax because compendium martial-arts styles require it]	BENEFIT:A successful unarmed attack roll allows you to make a second attack roll against a different opponent that is within the area that you threaten. This feat requires the full attack action.
Knock-Down	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General.Fighter.AttackOption	SOURCELONG:Sword & Fist	SOURCESHORT:SF	SOURCEPAGE:p.7	PRESTAT:1,STR=15	PRETOTALAB:2	PREABILITY:1,CATEGORY=FEAT,Improved Trip	DESC:Your mighty blows can knock foes off their feet. [Sword & Fist feat, included in 3.5 syntax because compendium martial-arts styles require it]	BENEFIT:Whenever you deal 10 or more points of damage to your opponent in melee with a single attack, you may make a trip attack as a free action against the same target. Use of this feat cannot be combined with Improved Trip to generate an extra attack, and successful use of this feat does not grant a further attack.
Lightning Fists	CATEGORY:FEAT	TYPE:General	SOURCELONG:Sword & Fist	SOURCESHORT:SF	SOURCEPAGE:p.7	PRESTAT:1,DEX=15	PREVARGTEQ:MonkLVL,4	DESC:Your skill and agility allow you to attempt a series of blindingly fast blows. [Sword & Fist feat, included in 3.5 syntax because compendium martial-arts styles require it]	BENEFIT:You can make two extra attacks in a round. All attacks made this round suffer a -5 attack penalty. This feat requires the full attack action. You cannot use Lightning Fists and flurry of blows at the same time.
